      "math_academy_id": "q-346078",
      "knowledge_point_id": "902a4c93-fd7e-5444-a9c0-0f3cbdb97cff",
      "knowledge_point": "Evaluating the Definite Integral of an Exponential Function",
      "problem": "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={e}^{x}\\,{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & ={e}^{3}-{e}^{0} \\\\  & ={e}^{3}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
