      "math_academy_id": "q-103652",
      "knowledge_point_id": "902a4c93-fd7e-5444-a9c0-0f3cbdb97cff",
      "knowledge_point": "Evaluating the Definite Integral of an Exponential Function",
      "problem": "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{2}{10}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{10}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{10}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}\\cdot {10}^{x}\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}({10}^{2}-{10}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}(100-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{99}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
