      "worked_solution": "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{8}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{8}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\cdot {8}^{x}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}({8}^{2}-{8}^{1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}(64-8) \\\\  & =\\frac{56}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
