      "knowledge_point_id": "92e86e5f-31cd-57ae-a142-023c816d0b33",
      "knowledge_point": "Evaluating the Definite Integral of a Trigonometric Function",
      "problem": "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}(-{csc}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}(-{csc}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}(-{csc}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =cot\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-cot\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}-\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-3}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
