      "problem": "${\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{3\\pi /4}(-{csc}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{3\\pi /4}(-{csc}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /3}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =-1-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+3}{3}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
